00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.310 align:start position:0%
 
okay so with spider-man no way home not  only breaking the multiverse internet  and the minds of every single marvel  maniac out there i thought i'd take a  look back at the movie that started it  all to talk about the best details in it  though it was made way before easter egg  hunters like myself obsessed over every  single shot in frame the movie is filled  to the brim with things most people miss  and we're still uncovering things about  it 20 years later the movie follows  spider-man as he goes toe-to-toe with  the green goblin and it's definitely a  battle for the ages several scenes  including the goblin's death are ripped  right out of the pages of the amazing  spider-man 1-2-2 in which he was impaled  by his own glider both norman osborne  and peter share somewhat of a father and  son relationship in the wake of uncle  ben's death but beyond this it's clear  norman wishes his son was more like  peter the idea of them being mirror  images of one another is shown during  the thanksgiving dinner in which the  pair wear the opposite's colours peter  wears a green shirt with a purple tie  whereas norman wears a blue shirt with a  red one going beyond this though harry  wears a mixture of both which somewhat  hints towards his fractured allegiances  throughout the entire trilogy there's  also several callbacks to this movie  with harry later down the line and when  peter first meets him he's wearing a  burgundy sweater with a t-shirt  underneath and a hoodie jacket over the  top in spider-man 3 when harry has  amnesia he also wears a similar set of  colours showing how his mind state has  gone back several years to the events of  this movie now willem dafoe really  embodies the role and it's easy to see  why they brought him back for no way  home the actor exudes a lot from his  facial expressions and during the scene  in which he acted against demira he did  these entirely in one take jumping back  and forth between the personas however  the creative team actually did something  really subtle to make it so that there  was an extra creepy factor to him and  when willem is playing the norman  osborne side he wears fake teeth that  makes his smile seem more in line  however when he's leaning into being the  goblin these are removed and we get  those awesome canine fang-like ones  creeping through his grin during the  green goblin jump scare that happens in  the film if you slow down the footage  you can also catch a second green goblin  standing in the background it's super  unnerving when you watch it and though  most people won't notice it it  subliminally gives the idea that the  goblin is supernatural however it also  might be hinting towards how a second  goblin will come down the line not too  far behind him in the form of harry when  he attacks j jonah jameson's office you  can also see that they've subtly painted  big black irises onto his mask which  gives them a bug-eyed look that's in  line with his costume from the comics  his home is also filled with the brain  with masks from ancient tribes and this  of course hints towards the goblin and  his subconscious now norman is very much  a tormented character and though we  never fully learn what happened to his  wife it's clear it was pretty bad just  before the balcony attack harry tells mj  that she should have worn black because  his father loves that colour and when  we're in the house we can catch a brief  glimpse out of mrs osborne who's wearing  a black dress at the dinner we then see  mj wearing black showing that she was  trying to impress norman even though it  didn't go down very well now norman says  that all women are beautiful until  they're snarling after your trust fund  like a pack of ravening wolves and thus  i think the woman in the portrait is  probably norman's mother this  thanksgiving dinner scene also has a lot  of similarities to the painting by  norman rockwell called freedom from want  i absolutely love how this shot is used  in a similar manner to demonstrate all  the characters coming together for one  final time before everyone ends up in  the crosshairs of the goblin now i feel  like we've been talking about the goblin  a lot and the true main character of  spider-man is of course well spider-man  see i told you it was amazing details on  this video now earlier in the movie  peter is bitten by a genetically altered  spider and we actually get some  foreshadowing of his powers on a screen  giving a cgi rendition of the arachnids  dna these include things like web  tensile strength spider strength jumping  speed spider sense precognition which  i'm guessing is the same as spider sense  and speed again the dna strands are  flying or red blue and green colours  that are of course associated with  spider-man and the green goblin we also  see a spider using its strength to  dangle a much heavier object by a web  string which somewhat foreshadows  spider-man holding onto the dangling  cable car later on in the movie now  peter also ends up taking a photograph  of mj and shouts new rock stars for  pointing out that this picture shows up  later in spider-man 2 in peter's  apartment peter ends up getting organic  webbing in the movie but at one point in  the film we can catch the web shooters  on his wrist which were originally  supposed to be a part of the plot but  these were later removed personally i  actually prefer the organic webbing as  what's the point of getting bit by a  spider if you can't shoot webs out your  ass now at one point in the film peter  eats lunch at school and if you look  closely at his hand you'll see a red  line coming down from the spider bite  indicating the track of its venom  speaking of venom robbie later brings up  to jameson their photographer eddie and  he says that he can't get a decent  photograph of spider-man this is of  course a reference to eddie brock and in  spider-man 3 he reuses peter's old  pictures touching them up with photoshop  in order to get paid now during this  lunch scene we watches peter catches  mary jane and also her lunch this moment  was actually done for real without any  cgi and though it apparently took 156  takes toby maguire actually managed to  do it the trick was pulled off using  adhesive which you can see on the bottom  of the apple and also magnets water fire  air and dirt [ __ ] magnets how do they  work well i'll explain and if you slow  down the footage you'll see that the  jelly actually bounces back on top of  the milk carton because of the magnet  that's laced on the inside of it now if  you look closely at peter's hand when he  shoots the webbing at the lunch tray  you'll also see that he makes the  spider-man web-firing gesture he doesn't  figure out until later on that this is  how you fire webs but i love that they  have this happening here to show exactly  why it went off now during this time  peter discovers his powers and he ends  up going to a rooftop where he tries to  fire his webs he says up up and away web  and also shazam the both of which are  references to superman and shazam  superman is also brought up by ant-may  later and i love the theory that in the  marvel universe our dc characters are  who are in the comic books and in the dc  universe marvels are the one on the page  this would explain why the flash has so  many marvel references in it and it's a  really nice fan theory now there's also  a moment where jameson looks through  peter's photos and he calls them all  crap i kind of think this might be a  reference to batman 1999 when the joker  does the same thing with vicki vales and  i promise that's the one reach for the  video what would you be they're all  riches now those dc ones are pretty  obvious easter eggs but this scene is  given a nod in spider-man homecoming  when ned asks peter how far he can shoot  his web and he says that if it was him  he'd just stand on the edge of a  building and shoot it to see how far it  goes now if you're enjoying the video  i'd massively appreciate the thumbs up  and i've got you for three more minutes  three minutes of bleed time but if you  want to stay around longer then please  subscribe who am i you sure you want to  know well i'm somewhat of an idiot  myself but the name's paul and this is  the heavy spoilers show now uncle ben's  death is a massive part of the  spider-man origin story and the  performance from cliff robertson was so  iconic that lines from his performance  were actually used years later in into  the spider-verse the conversation that  happens between peter and ben is really  impactful and it takes place in an  oldsmobile delta 88. the core has  appeared in a number of sam remy films  including the evil dead evil dead 2 dark  man army of darkness and also in drag me  to hell when peter exits if you slow  down the footage you can catch his red  hoodie hanging out the back of his  clothes too and he later go on to wear  this as part of his wrestling costume  the robber who apparently kills uncle  ben though i don't really count sandman  is doing it actually also appears in the  amazing spider-man once more showing  that yes it's all connected now during  this time we also see the origin story  of the green goblin and alongside him is  dr mendel strom who fans of the comics  might know as being a half man half  machine villain at one point in the  movie peter actually catches mary jane  working at the moon dan steiner and if  you've seen tiktik boom you'll know that  this location pops up in a 2 as being  where jonathan larson works at larson is  played by andrew garfield who of course  played spider-man and i love how this  all kind of ties together for trivia  fans also there's a cameo by lucy lulas  at one point who you may know is playing  xena the warrior princess now this movie  isn't perfect and there's faults in it  too like when peter is testing his  webbing as he shoots one at a lamp and  ends up smashing it and made a knocks  and when we cut back to a bigger shot of  the room we can see that the lampshade  is back where it was completely fixed  we'll forgive it though as he also  smashes a photo of himself ben and may  and later this shows up by ant-may's  bedside in a brand new photo frame  little touches like this and just  everything in the video that make this  movie great and i still have as much fun  with it now as it did all the way back  in 2002 i absolutely love it and if  there's any easter eggs in i miss then  make sure you comment below and let me  know we are in competition right now and  giving away three copies of the  spider-man 4k trilogies on the 30th of  december and all you have to do to be on  the chance of winning is like the video  make sure you subscribe with  notifications on and drop a comment  below with your thoughts on the video we  picked the comments at random at the end  of the month and the winners of the last  one are on screen right now so that's  you then message me on twitter  heavyspoilers if you want something else  to watch then make sure you check out  our breakdown of the spiderman across if  you want something else to watch then  make sure you check out our breakdown of  the spider-man across the spider-verse  first look which will be linked on  screen right now some really cool easter  eggs in it and lots of hidden details  that hint towards the movie's plot so  definitely go check it out right after  this if not then thanks for sitting  through the video i've been paul you've  been the best and i'll see you on the  next one take care peace

